{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>The fool.</b> There are also among men slothful fools who have no zeal and do not engage in work by which they might live; rather, they fold their hands and eat what they have, and are left without sustenance. And after he eats all that he has and does not labor to add more, it is as if he eats his own flesh, because he will die of hunger."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:28.876066324Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}